{"n": 100, "w": 1000, "h": 760, "img": "100.webp", "text": "ENGINE\n11-800b $14 M 88-3 S38\n\n11 00 ... Engine Oil Consumption\n\nDETERMINING OIL CONSUMPTION\n\nOil consumption can be measured for the first time after the car has been driven approximately\n7,500 km (4,500 miles). Oil consumption will be stable only after this distance. Measuring oll\nconsumption requires that the engine does not leak.\n\nPermissible oil consumption could be up to 0.15 liter/100 kilometers.\n\nPrecise consumption can be determined by weighing. Drain engine all having operating tem-\nperature. All 5 minutes drip time. Welgh and pour In specified amount of new engine oll.\nDrive car 1,000 km (600 miles). Drain engine oll at operating temperature and weigh. Allow 5\nminutes drip time. Engine oll density at room temperature Is approx. 0.9 km/cubic dm.\n\nExample: poured In oil — drained oll = consumed oll.\n4,500g - 3600g = 900g\n900 : density 0.9 = 1,000 cu. cm = 1 liter per 1,000 kilometers (600 miles).\n\nPossible Causes for Excessive Oil Consumption:\n\n1. Running-in process not completed.\n\n2. Seals for vaive stems damaged.\n\n3. Pistons seized.\n\n4, Piston rings Installed wrong, broken or worn.\n\n5. Excessive running clearance between valve stem and valve guide.", "words": [["ENGINE", 0.0213, 0.0187, 0.0737, 0.0334], ["11-800b", 0.0224, 0.0615, 0.0894, 0.0762], ["$14", 0.341, 0.0568, 0.3709, 0.0722], ["M", 0.5584, 0.0561, 0.5655, 0.0702], ["88-3", 0.5742, 0.0535, 0.6026, 0.0769], ["S38", 0.7754, 0.0548, 0.8044, 0.0689], ["11", 0.0244, 0.2086, 0.0366, 0.2219], ["00", 0.0432, 0.2079, 0.0589, 0.2219], ["...", 0.064, 0.2186, 0.0742, 0.2219], ["Engine", 0.0798, 0.2072, 0.125, 0.2259], ["Oil", 0.1301, 0.2072, 0.1474, 0.2219], ["Consumption", 0.1524, 0.2072, 0.2434, 0.2259], ["DETERMINING", 0.3445, 0.2533, 0.4426, 0.268], ["OIL", 0.4482, 0.2533, 0.4705, 0.268], ["CONSUMPTION", 0.4751, 0.2527, 0.5798, 0.268], ["Oil", 0.344, 0.3168, 0.3623, 0.3316], ["consumption", 0.3669, 0.3168, 0.4553